= In Committee: the Employment Bill

Backbenchers on the right have tabled amendments to ban the closed shop outright and to make unions liable for damages from secondary action. [+ employment_secretary +] says the amendments would wreck the bill and unite the unions against it.

- @amend_yes_employment1: Accept the amendments and toughen the bill.
- @amend_no_employment1: Keep the bill as it is.

@amend_yes_employment1
subtitle: Union power falls further. The wets and the TUC are furious.
on-arrival: right_dissent -= 3; dry_dissent -= 2; wet_dissent += 4; bill_employment1_tough = 1; bill_employment1 = 3; bill_employment1_amend = 2; bill_employment1_due = time + 1

The bill comes back from committee with teeth. The TUC General Council calls an emergency meeting.

@amend_no_employment1
subtitle: The right grumbles. Step by step was the plan.
on-arrival: right_dissent += 3; dry_dissent += 2; bill_employment1 = 3; bill_employment1_amend = 2; bill_employment1_due = time + 1

The amendments are voted down in committee, with the whips making sure the right-wingers on the committee are outnumbered.

@lords_employment1
title: The Lords Amend the Employment Bill
