= In Committee: the Employment Bill

Wets on the standing committee want to drop the clause that exposes union funds to damages, leaving the liability with individual officials. They say a union whose funds are seized will become a union of martyrs.

- @amend_yes_employment2: Accept the amendment.
- @amend_no_employment2: Reject it.

@amend_yes_employment2
subtitle: The bill is weaker. The wets are soothed; the dries are not.
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 3; dry_dissent += 4; bill_employment2_watered = 1; bill_employment2 = 3; bill_employment2_amend = 2; bill_employment2_due = time + 1

The clause goes. The unions are relieved, and the dries mutter that the government has lost its nerve.

@amend_no_employment2
subtitle: The wets will not forget it.
on-arrival: wet_dissent += 3; dry_dissent -= 2; rebellion += 0.3; bill_employment2 = 3; bill_employment2_amend = 2; bill_employment2_due = time + 1

The committee votes the amendment down by a single vote, after the whips change two of its members overnight.

