= The Lords Amend the Employment Bill

The House of Lords votes to hold closed-shop ballots every ten years instead of every five, which would leave most existing closed shops undisturbed for a decade.

- @lords_yes_employment2: Accept the Lords amendment.
- @lords_no_employment2: Overturn it in the Commons.

@lords_yes_employment2
subtitle: Union power falls a little less.
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 2; dry_dissent += 2; bill_employment2_watered = 1; bill_employment2_lords = 2; bill_employment2_due = time + 1

The government gives way. The bill is still the toughest union law for half a century. Royal Assent should follow within the month.

@lords_no_employment2
subtitle: The Lords may back down, or may not.
