@amend_housing
title: In Committee: the Housing Bill
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and in_campaign = 0 and bill_housing = 2 and bill_housing_amend = 1
new-page: true
face-image: img/events/commons_1970s.jpg

= In Committee: the Housing Bill

Members for rural and seaside seats want councils in National Parks and Areas of Outstanding Natural Beauty to be able to stop former council houses being sold on as holiday cottages.

- @amend_yes_housing: Accept the amendment.
- @amend_no_housing: Reject it.

@amend_yes_housing
subtitle: The shires are content.
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 2; dry_dissent += 1; bill_housing = 3; bill_housing_amend = 2; bill_housing_due = time + 1

Councils in the National Parks may now attach a covenant, so that a house bought under the right to buy can only be resold to someone who lives or works locally.

@amend_no_housing
subtitle: A few county members will rebel.
on-arrival: wet_dissent += 2; rebellion += 0.3; bill_housing = 3; bill_housing_amend = 2; bill_housing_due = time + 1

The amendment is defeated. The Lake District's member says the cottages will be full of weekenders from Manchester by 1985.

@lords_housing
title: The Lords Amend the Housing Bill
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and bill_housing = 4 and bill_housing_lords = 1
new-page: true
face-image: img/events/westminster.jpg

= The Lords Amend the Housing Bill

The House of Lords votes to exempt sheltered housing built for the elderly from the right to buy. Peers on all sides say councils that sell their old people's bungalows will never be able to replace them.

- @lords_yes_housing: Accept the Lords amendment.
- @lords_no_housing: Overturn it in the Commons.

@lords_yes_housing
subtitle: The wets approve. The right to buy is little changed.
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 2; right_dissent += 1; bill_housing_lords = 2; bill_housing_due = time + 1

The government accepts that housing designed for the elderly should be kept for them. Royal Assent should follow within the month.

@lords_no_housing
subtitle: Headlines about selling pensioners' homes. The Lords may back down.
on-arrival: thatcher_rating -= 1; wet_dissent += 2; dry_dissent -= 1; lords_key = "housing"
call: bill_insist

The whips bring the clause back to the Commons, and the government's majority reverses the Lords. [? if lords_gave_way = 1 : The peers decide not to press the point a second time, and the bill goes through as the government wanted. ?][? if lords_gave_way = 0 : The peers insist. After a month of messages between the two Houses, the government gives way to save the bill, with nothing to show for the delay. ?]

