= Royal Assent: the British Nationality Act

The British Nationality Act [+ year +] receives Royal Assent. Only British citizens now have the automatic right to live here. Critics say the Act was designed to keep people out, and in Hong Kong three million people discover that their passports no longer mean what they thought.

