= In Committee: the Rates Bill

Wets want the general power to cap every council in the country dropped, leaving only the selective scheme for the worst overspenders.

- @amend_yes_rates: Accept the amendment.
- @amend_no_rates: Reject it.

@amend_yes_rates
subtitle: The wets are soothed. Ratepayers get less relief.
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 3; right_dissent += 2; bill_rates_watered = 1; bill_rates = 3; bill_rates_amend = 2; bill_rates_due = time + 1

The general power goes. Only the councils named each year by the Environment Secretary will be capped.

@amend_no_rates
subtitle: The wets dig in.
on-arrival: wet_dissent += 3; right_dissent -= 1; rebellion += 0.5; bill_rates = 3; bill_rates_amend = 2; bill_rates_due = time + 1

The amendment is defeated. The county councils, many of them Conservative, start to worry.

