= The Lords Amend the Rates Bill

The House of Lords votes to make the Environment Secretary consult each council before capping its rate, and to let councils appeal.

- @lords_yes_rates: Accept the Lords amendment.
- @lords_no_rates: Overturn it in the Commons.

@lords_yes_rates
subtitle: A delay in each case, nothing worse.
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 2; bill_rates_lords = 2; bill_rates_due = time + 1

The government accepts the duty to consult. Councils will be able to make their case before the cap comes down. Royal Assent should follow within the month.

