= In Committee: the Local Government Bill

London Conservatives want a new elected body to run the capital's strategic services, its roads, its fire brigade and its planning, once the GLC is gone.

- @amend_yes_glc: Accept the amendment.
- @amend_no_glc: Reject it.

@amend_yes_glc
subtitle: The wets approve. The right asks what the point was.
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 3; right_dissent += 3; bill_glc_watered = 1; bill_glc = 3; bill_glc_amend = 2; bill_glc_due = time + 1

London will get a smaller, elected strategic authority in place of the GLC. Livingstone says he will stand for it.

@amend_no_glc
subtitle: London Tories will rebel.
on-arrival: wet_dissent += 3; right_dissent -= 2; rebellion += 0.5; bill_glc = 3; bill_glc_amend = 2; bill_glc_due = time + 1

The amendment is defeated. London's services will be run by joint boards of the boroughs.

@lords_glc
title: The Lords Defeat the Local Government Bill
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and bill_glc = 4 and bill_glc_lords = 1
new-page: true
