= The Lords Defeat the Local Government Bill

The House of Lords votes down the plan to cancel next year's elections and replace the councillors with nominees. Peers of every party say it is wrong to abolish an election before Parliament has abolished the council.

- @lords_yes_glc: Let the councillors serve on until abolition.
- @lords_no_glc: Overturn the Lords in the Commons.

@lords_yes_glc
subtitle: Livingstone stays at County Hall a little longer.
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 2; thatcher_rating -= 1; bill_glc_lords = 2; bill_glc_due = time + 1

The government gives way. The councillors elected in 1981 will serve until the council disappears, and Livingstone gets another year on the roof of County Hall. Royal Assent should follow within the month.

@lords_no_glc
subtitle: The rebellion grows. The Lords may back down.
on-arrival: rebellion += 1; wet_dissent += 3; c1_con -= 1; lords_key = "glc"
call: bill_insist

