= In Committee: the Police and Criminal Evidence Bill

Backbenchers want interviews at police stations to be tape-recorded, and every suspect to have the right to see a solicitor.

- @amend_yes_pace: Accept the amendment.
- @amend_no_pace: Reject it.

@amend_yes_pace
subtitle: The Liberals and the wets approve. The police federation does not.
on-arrival: lib_relation += 3; wet_dissent -= 2; right_dissent += 2; bill_pace = 3; bill_pace_amend = 2; bill_pace_due = time + 1

Tape-recorders will be installed in every interview room, and the duty solicitor will be a phone call away.

@amend_no_pace
subtitle: The right approves. The civil liberties lobby does not.
on-arrival: lib_relation -= 2; wet_dissent += 2; right_dissent -= 1; bill_pace = 3; bill_pace_amend = 2; bill_pace_due = time + 1

The amendment is defeated. The police will keep their own notes of interviews, as they always have.

