@amend_telecoms
title: In Committee: the Telecommunications Bill
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and in_campaign = 0 and bill_telecoms = 2 and bill_telecoms_amend = 1
new-page: true
face-image: img/events/commons_1970s.jpg

= In Committee: the Telecommunications Bill

Backbenchers from rural seats want a guarantee that a private British Telecom will keep the call boxes and the lines to the remote farms that will never make it a penny.

- @amend_yes_telecoms: Accept the amendment.
- @amend_no_telecoms: Reject it.

@amend_yes_telecoms
subtitle: The shires are content.
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 2; dry_dissent += 1; bill_telecoms = 3; bill_telecoms_amend = 2; bill_telecoms_due = time + 1

British Telecom's licence will oblige it to keep a universal service, including the red telephone boxes in the villages.

@amend_no_telecoms
subtitle: The regulator can sort it out later.
on-arrival: wet_dissent += 2; dry_dissent -= 1; rebellion += 0.2; bill_telecoms = 3; bill_telecoms_amend = 2; bill_telecoms_due = time + 1

The amendment is defeated. The new regulator will have to make the case for the call boxes.

@lords_telecoms
title: The Lords Amend the Telecommunications Bill
